<nav><a href="./">← Chloe reads Jon</a><span>A small window into a large mystery</span></nav>
<header class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">An illustrated reflection · No timer. No score.</div><h1>Beyond<br>the <em>postcard.</em></h1></div><p class="lede">Green grass. Blue sky. Billowy clouds.<br>Beautiful, yes. But what if the heart of heaven isn’t the scenery?</p></header>
<section class="experience" aria-label="Explore five signs of communion">
<div class="gallery"><div class="scene" id="scene">
<img src="?art=1" alt="A painted open archway overlooking green hills, with a welcoming chair, a shared table, two friends listening, paths meeting in light, and hands sharing water." width="1536" height="1024">
<div class="veil"></div>
<button class="pin" style="--x:12%;--y:60%" data-i="0" aria-label="1. The open door" aria-pressed="false">1</button>
<button class="pin" style="--x:50%;--y:72%" data-i="1" aria-label="2. The shared table" aria-pressed="false">2</button>
<button class="pin" style="--x:78%;--y:60%" data-i="2" aria-label="3. Face to face" aria-pressed="false">3</button>
<button class="pin" style="--x:53%;--y:32%" data-i="3" aria-label="4. Into the light" aria-pressed="false">4</button>
<button class="pin" style="--x:80%;--y:85%" data-i="4" aria-label="5. A cup of water" aria-pressed="false">5</button>
</div><div class="caption"><span>Touch a numbered detail. Follow the welcome.</span><span id="count">0 / 5 opened</span></div></div>
<div class="reading"><div class="counter" id="chapter">Begin anywhere</div><div id="words" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><h2>A view is lovely.<br>A welcome is different.</h2><p>Explore five little details in the painting. Each opens a way to think about Jon’s surprising thought: heaven is communion with God, not simply a wonderful destination.</p><p class="question">If you could enter the most beautiful place imaginable, but could never love or be loved there, would it be enough?</p></div><button class="next" id="next">Open the first detail →</button><div class="progress" aria-label="Exploration progress"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="quote"><div class="small">The thought behind the window<br><br>Catechism of the Catholic Church<br>Paragraph 260 · quoted by Jon</div><blockquote>“The ultimate end of the whole divine economy is the entry of God’s creatures into the perfect unity of the Blessed Trinity.”<cite>“But even now we are called to be a dwelling for the Most Holy Trinity.”</cite></blockquote></section>
<section class="keepsake" id="keepsake" hidden><div class="print-title">Beyond the Postcard</div><div class="eyebrow">Bring a little of the welcome home</div><h2>Not just someday.<br>One small opening, today.</h2><p id="summary">You opened every window. Choose one glimpse to carry into the ordinary day.</p><label for="intention">Today, I can make room for love by…</label><textarea id="intention" maxlength="500" placeholder="Giving someone my undivided attention for five minutes."></textarea><p class="quiet" style="font-size:14px">Your words stay on this page, not on a server. Save a text keepsake if you want to keep them.</p><div class="actions"><button id="save">Save my keepsake ↓</button><button id="print" class="plain">Print this window</button><button id="restart" class="plain">Look again ↺</button></div><div class="notice" id="notice" role="status"></div></section>
<footer><div class="note">Inspired by Jon’s <a href="?source=1">On Heaven</a> (2013).<br>A poetic illustration, not a literal map of heaven. Heaven is the fulfilment of life in God; these ordinary scenes are only glimpses of communion.</div><div>Original artwork created for this window.<br><a href="./">Explore the collection →</a></div></footer>
